@startuml MiniRedis_Architecture
!theme vibrant
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #E9ECEF

title MiniRedis Architecture & Component Interaction Diagram

package "External Clients" {
    [redis-cli] as Client1
    [Python redis-py] as Client2
    [Node ioredis] as Client3
}

package "MiniRedis Core Server Engine (C++17)" {

    package "Networking & Reactor Layer" {
        [Listening Socket\n(Port: 6379)] as ServerSocket
        [EventLoop Reactor\n(Linux epoll_wait)] as Reactor
        [Connection Handle\n(Read & Write Buffers)] as ConnMgr
    }

    package "Protocol & Dispatcher Layer" {
        [RespParser\n(RESP2 Stream Parser)] as Parser
        [Router Engine\n(Command Dispatcher)] as Router
    }

    package "Storage & Persistence Engine" {
        database "Database Engine\n(std::unordered_map)]" as DB
        [Value Container\n(std::variant + TTL)] as Val
        file "AofEngine\n(appendonly.aof Log)" as AOF
        [Active Expiration Timer\n(100ms epoll timeout)] as Purger
    }
}

' Component Connections
Client1 <--> Reactor : Non-Blocking TCP Sockets
Client2 <--> Reactor : Non-Blocking TCP Sockets
Client3 <--> Reactor : Non-Blocking TCP Sockets

Reactor --> ServerSocket : Accept New Client Connections
Reactor --> ConnMgr : Dispatch EPOLLIN (Read) & EPOLLOUT (Write) Events

ConnMgr <--> Parser : Pass Input Buffer / Receive RespValue
Parser --> Router : Forward Decoded RESP Command Array
Router --> DB : Execute Key-Value Operations
DB *-- Val : Stores Key -> Value Objects
Router --> AOF : Write-Ahead Append (Mutating Commands)
Reactor ..> Purger : 100ms Timeout Trigger
Purger --> DB : Purge Expired TTL Keys

@enduml
